    "causal_summary": "The per-lineage worktree mechanism cost 1.6 GB and about 22 seconds per lane, existed only to make write attribution exact, and attribution is not a requirement: the operator's need is that a lane never halts on a neighbour's write and that no output is lost, which preserve-by-default plus the never-fatal untracked rule already meet",
